    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
    "original_text": "Fan Chen,Sinho Chewi,Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang supply Appendix D.1 spectral-calculus background. This ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 corollary uses pinned Mathlib CFC and local complexification;it is not a separately printed theorem.\nFor every measurable space Ω and every measure μ,let G,D be bounded real linear operators on real L²(μ). Assume G,D positive:selfadjoint with nonnegative quadratic form. If G²D=DG²,then GD=DG. No probability,finite measure,finite-dimensional L²,nontriviality or caller CFC instance is required. This ASTIS auxiliary consequence of unique positive-root functional calculus is not a separately printed PBPS theorem. Its actual paper consumer internally proves D=I+T positive and G² commuting with D;these are not extra paper premises.\nPBPS2609.06905v1 Appendix D.1 spectral calculus background;ASTIS positive real-L2 square commutation corollary for B23/B21.",
    "text_sha256": "509e73b850c3c7a4f0600ba00a4fa80bc1b2b8ab76cf31bb8d9520d1a3219e9b"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareCommute.positive_square_commutation",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/L2RealSquareCommute.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (G D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ)\n    (hG : G.IsPositive) (hD : D.IsPositive)\n    (hCommute : Commute (G*G) D) : Commute G D",
    "statement_sha256": "c58d138c8c2d371b326aefbec51d51f2405985901a2370714726484487f3a892",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Lp ℝ 2 μ is the Hilbert space of real-valued square-integrable classes for the stated measure;→L[ℝ] means bounded real-linear operators. IsPositive means symmetric with nonnegative quadratic form. Commute A B means A*B=B*A;operator multiplication is composition.",
      "All witnesses following existential quantifiers are concluded data,not public assumptions. Exact initial caller binders delimit the input conditions."
    ],
    "statement_representation": {
      "kind": "direct-header",
      "actual_header": "theorem positive_square_commutation\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (G D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ)\n    (hG : G.IsPositive) (hD : D.IsPositive)\n    (hCommute : Commute (G*G) D) : Commute G D\n",
      "private_definition": "",
      "expanded_header": "theorem positive_square_commutation\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (G D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ)\n    (hG : G.IsPositive) (hD : D.IsPositive)\n    (hCommute : Commute (G*G) D) : Commute G D\n",
