        {
          "title": "Commute with the same positive square root",
          "text": "The unique positive root of Gc² is Gc. Commutation with the argument passes to its continuous functional calculus.",
          "formula": "\\sqrt{G_{\\mathbb C}^2}=G_{\\mathbb C},\\quad[G_{\\mathbb C}^2,D_{\\mathbb C}]=0\\Rightarrow[G_{\\mathbb C},D_{\\mathbb C}]=0.",
